ashington Football Team That Must Not Be Named". NPR. Archived from the original on June 2, 2021. Retrieved June 1, 2021.\n- ^ Breech, John (August 23, 2014). "ESPN updates its policy regarding use of Redskins team name". CBS Sports. Archived from the original on December 1, 2017. Retrieved June 1, 2021.\n- ^ Connolly, Matt (May 22, 2014). "50 Senators Call on Washington Football Team to Change Name". MotherJones.com. Archived from the original on June 2, 2021. Retrieved June 1, 2021.\n- ^ Keim, John (July 14, 2020). "How the events of 2020 forced the Washington NFL team\'s name change". ESPN. Archived from the original on July 14, 2020. Retrieved July 15, 2020.\n- ^ McDonald, Scott (July 1, 2020). "Washington Redskins Urged to Lose Name, or Millions in Sponsorships". Newsweek. Archived from the original on July 3, 2020. Retrieved July 15, 2020.\n- ^ Clarke, Liz (July 10, 2020). "In private letter to Redskins, FedEx said it will remove signage if name isn\'t changed". The Washington Post. Archived from the original on July 14, 2020. Retrieved July 15, 2020.\n- ^ "Amazon to pull Redskins merchandise while team mulls nickname change". ESPN. Associated Press. July 8, 2020. Archived from the original on July 15, 2020. Retrieved July 15, 2020.\n- ^ Tyko, Kelly (July 6, 2020). "Walmart, Target, Dick\'s Sporting Goods pull Washington Redskins items as team evaluates name". USA Today. Archived from the original on July 14, 2020. Retrieved July 15, 2020.\n- ^ Patra, Kevin (July 13, 2020). "Washington retiring nickname, logo; new nickname TBD". NFL. Archived from the original on July 16, 2020. Retrieved July 16, 2020.\n- ^ "Statement From The Washington Redskins Football Team". Commanders.com (Press release). July 13, 2020. Archived from the original on July 13, 2020. Retrieved February 2, 2022.\n- ^ Walker, Jackson (September 25, 2023). "EXCLUSIVE: Washington Commanders sued by Native American organization trying to restore old team name". NBC Montana. Retrieved November 14, 2023.\n- ^ Mordowanec, Nick (September 25, 2023). "Washington Commanders Accused of Defaming Native Americans in Name Fight". Newsweek. Retrieved November 14, 2023.\n- ^ Szpaller, Keila (May 15, 2024). "Daines advocates that Washington Commanders \'make it right\' with Wetzel family". Daily Montanan. Retrieved May 16, 2024.\n- ^ Caldwell, Dave (December 7, 2021). "A Native American designed Washington\'s logo. Now his family want it back". The Guardian. Retrieved July 6, 2024.\n- ^ Coley, Joanne (November 27, 2024). "Commanders Urged to Consider Bringing Back Redskins Logo". Sports Illustrated. Archived from the original on November 27, 2024. Retrieved November 27, 2024.\n- ^ Salguero, Armando (November 24, 2024). "NFL And Congress Discussing Return Of The Washington Redskins Logo". OutKick. Retrieved November 27, 2024.\n- ^ Demissie, Hannah. "Trump \'won\'t make a deal\' with Washington Commanders if team refuses to change name". ABC News. Retrieved July 22, 2025.\n- ^ "Trump threatens to hold up stadium deal if Washington Commanders don\'t switch back to Redskins". AP News. July 20, 2025. Retrieved July 22, 2025.\n- ^ Trotta, Daniel; Trotta, Daniel (July 21, 2025). "Trump threatens Washington stadium deal unless NFL team readopts Redskins name". Reuters. Retrieved July 22, 2025.\n- ^ "The Cowboys-Redskins rivalry redefines the term \'fight song\'". FOX Sports. Retrieved April 7, 2008.[permanent dead link]\n- ^ "NFL History 1951–1960". National Football League. Archived from the original on February 9, 2007. Retrieved April 7, 2008.\n- ^ a b c d Toomay, Pat. "A rivalry for a song ... and chicken feed". ESPN.com. Archived from the original on April 9, 2008. Retrieved February 1, 2022.\n- ^ Coppinger, Mike (November 25, 2016). "Cowboys-Redskins was most-watched regular-season game in Fox history". USA Today. Archived from the original on December 20, 2016. Retrieved February 3, 2017.\n- ^ "All Matchups, Washington Commanders vs. Dallas Cowboys". Pro Football Reference. Retrieved January 5, 2025.\n- ^ "All Matchups, Washington Commanders vs. Philadelphia Eagles". Pro Football Reference. Retrieved January 5, 2025.\n- ^ "All Matchups, Washington Commanders vs. New York Giants". Pro Football Reference. Retrieved January 5, 2025.\n- ^ "Are The Ravens and Redskins Really Rivals?". FOX Sports. June 30, 2017. Retrieved August 10, 2024.\n- ^ Zimmerlee, Connor (July 21, 2023). "Commanders\' Sale Spawns Rivalry With Ravens?". Sports Illustrated. Retrieved August 10, 2024.\n- ^ Bumbaca, Chris (August 22, 2023). "Baltimore Ravens\' preseason win streak ends vs. Washington Commanders". USA TODAY. Retrieved August 10, 2024.\n- ^ "All Matchups, Washington Commanders vs. Baltimore Ravens". Pro Football Reference. Retrieved October 14, 2024.\n- ^ Shapiro, Leonard; Maske, Mark (December 8, 1993). "BALTIMORE NFL BACKERS SAY COOKE UNDERCUT EFFORTS TO LAND TEAM". Washington Post. Retrieved August 10, 2024.\n- ^ Howard, Johnette (January 31, 2013). "Howard: Cleveland, Baltimore football history could have changed at meeting". ESPN.com. Retrieved August 10, 2024.\n- ^ "Tagliabue Couldn\'t Stop Baltimore!". July 31, 2015.\n- ^ a b "Theismann\'s No. 7 taken out of circulation again". USA Today. May 13, 2002. Archived from the original on December 7, 2008. Retrieved February 19, 2008.\n- ^ "Theismann gives Haskins permission to wear no. 7". ESPN. May 1, 2019. Archived from the original on May 2, 2019. Retrieved May 2, 2019.\n- ^ Keim, John (June 24, 2020). "Redskins removing name of former owner George Preston Marshall from Ring of Fame". ESPN. Archived from the original on June 26, 2020. Retrieved June 24, 2020.\n- ^ "Ring of Fame". Commanders.com. Archived from the original on February 2, 2022. Retrieved February 2, 2022.\n- ^ "Washington Commanders to induct Mike Bass into Ring of Fame during 2022 season opener". Commanders.com. Archived from the original on August 4, 2022. Retrieved August 4, 2022.\n- ^ a b c d "80 Greatest Redskins". Commanders.com