answer=The documents say that in **1980** the first overall pick in the NFL draft was **Billy Sims, a running back**, and he was chosen by the **Detroit Lions**: “**With the first overall pick of the draft, the Detroit Lions selected running back Billy Sims.**”

So, in the year Ronald Reagan was first elected president, the player was **Billy Sims**, and the team was the **Detroit Lions**.
